  "description_html": "Diagram of divergences in hand elements of the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Theropod\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Theropod\">theropod</a> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Dinosaurs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dinosaurs\">dinosaurs</a> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosauridae\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosauridae\">Tyrannosauridae</a> ( here <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Albertosaurus\" title=\"Albertosaurus\">Albertosaurus</a></i>, <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tarbosaurus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tarbosaurus\">Tarbosaurus</a></i>, <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Daspletosaurus\" title=\"Daspletosaurus\">Daspletosaurus</a></i> and <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus_rex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus rex\">Tyrannosaurus rex</a></i> ). although very similar in basic, ther is differences in the matter of the construction of the arm <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Bones\" title=\"Bones\">bones</a> and the stunted <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Metacarpal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Metacarpal (page does not exist)\">metacarpal</a> III. \n<ul><li>Not to scale, but all the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Arm\" title=\"Arm\">arms</a> are about the same size (except <i>Tarbosaurus</i>, which has the smallest forelimb elements of any <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurids\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurids\">Tyrannosaurid</a>). As <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Coelurosaurs&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Coelurosaurs (page does not exist)\">coelurosaurs</a>, some <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurids\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosaurids\">tyrannosaurids</a> have very hollow arm bones, which <i>may</i> have made them fragile and could not have been used for heavy loads. They also have <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Metarcarpal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Metarcarpal (page does not exist)\">metarcarpal</a> III fused with metacarpal II. <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosaurus\" title=\"Tyrannosaurus\">Tyrannosaurus</a></i> on the other hand has very thick arm bones, and the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Metacarpal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Metacarpal (page does not exist)\">metacarpal</a> III is detaching from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Metacarpal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Metacarpal (page does not exist)\">metacarpal</a> II. This indicates that it may had a special function in the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Hand\" title=\"Hand\">hand</a>.</li></ul>",
  "categories": "Self-published work|PD-self|Tyrannosauroidea anatomy"
 }
